# rx26_uav udev rules — stable device names + permissions.
# Install with install_udev.sh.
#
# Only the devices ACTUALLY ABOARD get a rule. A symlink for hardware that is
# not on the airframe is worse than no symlink: it makes a config file look
# satisfied while pointing at whatever else happened to enumerate.
#
# CONFIRMED ABOARD 2026-09-02 (Ekko): CubePilot CubeOrange+, 2dae:1058,
# serial 430021000951343034383930. The earlier candidate list (26ac, 1209:5741,
# 1209:5740) has been pruned — none of those boards is on this airframe.
#
# --- Pixhawk (autopilot). Owned EXCLUSIVELY by MAVProxy; everything else uses
#     the UDP rebroadcast on 14541/14540. The symlink exists so
#     uav-mavproxy.service never chases ttyACM numbering.
#
#     !! ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="00" IS LOAD-BEARING. !!
#     The CubeOrange+ enumerates TWO CDC-ACM interfaces from ONE USB device:
#       if00 -> the MAVLink port (SERIAL0). This is the one MAVProxy needs.
#       if02 -> a second interface that answers no MAVLink at all.
#     A rule matching only ATTRS{idVendor} matches BOTH, so both interfaces
#     claim the symlink and whichever udev happens to process last wins. That
#     is a coin flip ON EVERY BOOT. Observed 2026-09-02: before a reboot the
#     symlink landed on if00 and the aircraft worked; after the reboot it
#     landed on if02 and MAVProxy sat at "no link" forever with a perfectly
#     healthy USB cable. Diagnosing that in a field is expensive.
#
#     Verify after any change to this file:
#       ls -l /dev/uav-pixhawk        # must resolve to the if00 ttyACM
#       udevadm info -q property -n /dev/uav-pixhawk | grep INTERFACE_NUM
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2dae", ATTRS{idProduct}=="1058", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="00", SYMLINK+="uav-pixhawk", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"

# --- 915MHz telemetry radio (SiK, Silabs CP210x). OPTIONAL: the aircraft flies
#     without it, so install_udev.sh does not warn when it is absent.
#     NOTE: Ekko's ground-side radio is an FTDI FT231X (0403:6015), not CP210x.
#     This rule is for a Silabs radio carried ON the aircraft, if one ever is.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="10c4", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ea60", SYMLINK+="uav-telem", MODE="0660", GROUP="dialout"

# --- NO RULE for the ELRS receiver. It talks CRSF to the Pixhawk's RC input,
#     not USB to the Jetson — it never enumerates here.
#
# --- NO camera rule. The SIYI A8 mini is an ETHERNET device (192.168.144.25 on
#     enP8p1s0), not USB. Nothing to name here.
